/viaf.org/viaf/242059233","http://viaf.org/viaf/125499078","https://d-nb.info/gnd/4000556-2","http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n80061791","http://data.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb11863530z","http://data.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb15238583n","http://data.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb11938556d","http://www.idref.fr/027316866/id","http://www.idref.fr/026375680/id","http://id.ndl.go.jp/auth/ndlna/00562068","http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D004534","https://www.freebase.com/m/02k54","https://g.co/kg/m/02k54","http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/Z01.058.266.317","http://datos.bne.es/resource/XX450764","https://livedata.bibsys.no/authority/90074621","https://sws.geonames.org/357994/","http://vocab.getty.edu/tgn/7016833","http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1208755","http://www.yso.fi/onto/yso/p105841","http://babelnet.org/rdf/s00005255n","http://nomisma.org/id/egypt","http://zbw.eu/stw/descriptor/17745-0","http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept706","http://www.yso.fi/onto/ysa/Y105841","http://dbpedia.org/resource/Egypt"]}],"providedCHOs":[{"about":"/item/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_CI260"}],"proxies":[{"about":"/proxy/europeana/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_CI260","dcCoverage":{"def":["http://data.europeana.eu/place/32"]},"dcIdentifier":{"def":["http://data.collectienederland.nl/resource/document/rijksmuseum-van-oudheden/CI260"]},"proxyIn":["/aggregation/europeana/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_CI260"],"proxyFor":"/item/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_CI260","lineage":["/proxy/provider/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_CI260"],"edmType":"IMAGE","europeanaProxy":true},{"about":"/proxy/provider/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_CI260","dcCoverage":{"def":["Egypte"]},"dcDate":{"def":["Grieks-Romeinse Periode; Romeinse keizertijd 30 v.Chr.-640 n.Chr."]},"dcDescription":{"def":["krokodil ; mummie The animal has been wrapped in a piece of medium-fine cloth of pale brown colour, held in position by means of some loops of yarn. This layer is visible only along the sides of the back and through holes in the ventral side. These holes also show a number of strips of papyrus rind (?) inserted for reinforcement. The ventral side of this package was then covered with various longitudinal strips of linen, glued into position using gum arabic or another adhesive. Along each side these strips form three neatly overlapping pleats of 0.4-0.8 cm width, and there are seven similar pleats along the spine. These pleated bands are held in position by three transverse straps: one behind the head, one at the point of greatest width, and one about halfway the length of the crocodile. The dorsal pleats have a remarkable bleached appearance, whereas some remains of dark brown linen (now largely decayed but still visible under some of the transverse straps and on the left shoulder) suggest that there may have been more transverse elements of a contrasting colour, thus forming a proper checked pattern. The tail is wrapped in a single piece of medium-fine linen (warp-faced tabby weave, c. 10 x 34 threads/cm2), slightly damaged at the tip. The head is covered with various longitudinal strips, applied in such a way that the eyes are recessed. Along the rims, another layer of dark brown linen can again be observed, whereas the pupils are painted in black. A single horizontal band indicates the mouth of the animal."]},"dcIdentifier":{"def":["CI 260"]},"dcRights":{"def":["Creative Commons By-licensie: bron: Rijksmuseum van Oudheden, Leiden"]},"dcSubject":{"def":["krokodil"]},"dcTitle":{"def":["mummie ; reptiel ; dierenmummie ; krokodil"]},"dcType":{"def":["mummie ; reptiel ; dierenmummie ; krokodil"]},"dctermsCreated":{"def":["Grieks-Romeinse Periode; Romeinse keizertijd 30 v.Chr.-640 n.Chr."]},"dctermsExtent":{"def":["35 x 8,1 x 5,3 cm"]},"dctermsIsReferencedBy":{"def":["Leemans, Description raisonnée (1840) N 33 Boeser, Catalogus (1907) E.XLV.28 Falke, T.H.M., Essays Te Velde (Groninge